### Manual API tests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (free).
### Click "Send Request" above any request. Start the API first (see README).

@base = http://localhost:8000

### 1. Register an employee
POST {{base}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "employee@example.com",
  "full_name": "Ella Employee",
  "password": "Str0ngPassw0rd!"
}

### 2. Log in - copy the access_token from the response into the @token line below
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "employee@example.com",
  "password": "Str0ngPassw0rd!"
}

###
@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 3. Who am I?
GET {{base}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Create the example ticket from the project spec
POST {{base}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Unable to connect to company Wi-Fi",
  "description": "My laptop cannot join the office network since Monday morning.",
  "category": "Network",
  "priority": "Medium"
}

### 5. List my tickets (try adding ?q=wi-fi&status=Open)
GET {{base}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Add a comment
POST {{base}}/api/tickets/1/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "I have already tried restarting the laptop." }

### 7. SECURITY CHECK - an employee must be refused (403) here
GET {{base}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. SECURITY CHECK - SQL injection text is treated as plain text (0 results, no error)
GET {{base}}/api/tickets?q=' OR '1'='1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Log out (the token stops working immediately)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
